{"seq":21,"id":"agent.run","props":{"input":"create some nations.  there are two large empires and 5 smaller monarchies.","scene":"opening"},"invocation":"agent.run(input='create some nations.  there are two large empires and 5 smaller monarchies.' scene='opening')","source":"ui","mutating":true,"gitHead":"363cbebd6b03c82e9118741e3b0b60f8a4ea1633","gitDirty":true,"startedAt":"2026-08-18T05:49:29.859Z","finishedAt":"2026-08-18T05:51:03.428Z","status":"ok","message":"Done — added **wiki/world/nations.md**, validated clean and committed as `5e41e45b`. It fits the Aetherwork world:\n\n**Two Empires**\n- **The Ferran Ascendancy** — elder empire of iron and law; heartland of the Regulen Concord, ruled by the Iron Diet under a ceremonial Ascendant; builds and sells the world's Governors. Capital: Cograuncy.\n- **The Vashan Dominion** — younger conquest-empire embracing the Kiln-Sworn and ungoverned Vash; ruled by a warrior-Overlord. Capital: Cinderhold. Locked in cold war with Ferra.\n\n**Five Monarchies**\n- **Halcyon Reach** — neutral highland haven of the Loomwrights; its queen brokers peace.\n- **The Marches of Cindral** — volcanic border-kingdom rich in aether ore, courted by the Dominion.\n- **The Saltbound Crownland** — maritime trade-monarchy controlling the choke-point straits.\n- **The Grey Principality of Vorn** — cold, pious north where the Assayers hold sway.\n- **The Free Duchy of Amberline** — small, rich, canal-laced duchy of banks and spy-guilds.\n\nEach ties back to the Orders and the Sela/Vash divide, with fault lines noted. Want me to sketch a map concept, or wire any of these into characters or locations next?","commits":[{"repo":"C:\\dev\\visualnovel\\examples\\test4","sha":"4c459cc01d18b1f0e3fdea7b498477015402f84b"}]}
